      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# dsh-cost\n\n**Account balance and cost statistics** pill for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness). It adds a pill at the right-hand end of the official stats row below the session composer, combining three readings: the billing period (peak / off-peak, colour-coded), the account balance, and the current session cost. Clicking the pill expands a per-session breakdown — cache-hit input, cache-miss input and output amounts, cost per model, the successful web search / web fetch call counts and their per-request fee (billed from 2026-11-01), and the token and web-call cost of the subagent sessions this session spawned (at any depth). The cost side needs no credentials; the balance side needs a DeepSeek API key.\n\n> Community plugin. Not affiliated with, endorsed by, or shipped by DeepSeek.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n![Cost pill at the right-hand end of the stats row](assets/screenshots/pill-101c.png)\n\n![Breakdown popup](assets/screenshots/dialog-101c.png)\n\n## Features\n\n- **Rightmost pill in the stats row**: registers into `conversation.composer.dock` with `order: 2`, after both official stats pills (`activity` = 0, `usage` = 1). The period reads `Peak` or `Off-peak`, and a red / green dot distinguishes them.\n- **Popup breakdown**: billing period, account balance, current session cost, the cost split by bucket — cache-hit input, cache-miss input (cache writes included), output — a per-model breakdown whenever the host can fold one, and the session's successful web search / web fetch call counts and fee when it made such calls. Subagent spend is not a separate line: it is folded into every amount above; when subagents exist, the session-cost label reads \"(incl. subagents)\" and a small note says how many sessions are included.\n- **Subagent spend included**: every descendant subagent session (identified by the `origin: subagent` header lineage, including subagents of subagents) has its token usage and web call fees folded into the existing fields — total, the three token buckets, the web rows and the per-model rows. A user fork is an independent conversation and never counts. Running subagents are read from memory; closed ones are read from their persisted logs through the session-query service and cached.\n- **Official pricing**: the 2026-09-10 price cut and the pro→flash routing are both modelled. While the session is attached, usage is folded per request, so a session spanning a price change, a routing change or a peak boundary never mixes two rate tables. The Search / Fetch call fee follows the official 2026-10-17 notice: ¥5 per 1,000 successful requests (¥0.005 each), with failures, empty searches and timeouts free, billed for DeepSeek Harness server-side tool calls from 2026-11-01 00:00 Beijing on; the plugin prices each call at its own moment and shows calls inside the free period as \"Free\".\n- **Peak / off-peak clock**: workday windows `09:00–12:00` and `14:00–18:00`; everything else, weekends and statutory holidays bill off-peak all day (including a weekend that holiday adjustment turns into a workday). The built-in 2026 PRC holiday table can be replaced through `Config.holidays`.\n- **Rates follow official pricing**: the rate table ships inside the plugin and is refreshed with plugin releases.\n- **Works without an API key**: installs signed in with a DeepSeek account still see the billing period and the session cost; only the balance is absent.\n- **No credentials stored**: the key is resolved through dsh's credentials seam, used in-process, and never written to disk.\n- **Bilingual**: 20 dictionary entries under the `cost-stats` namespace, Chinese and English, following the app locale.\n- **Host route only**: the browser half reads the host route `/api/dsh-balance` (once per session step plus a 60 s poll) and never contacts a third party.\n- **No local state**: nothing is persisted; uninstalling leaves no data behind.\n- **Native behaviour**: positioning and outside-dismiss reuse the official `ui-primitives` helpers (`useAnchoredPosition`, `useDismissOnOutsidePointer`).\n\n## Requirements\n\n- DeepSeek Harness (dsh) `>= 0.2.1-rc.2`.\n- A DeepSeek **API key** if you want the balance. It is resolved through dsh's credentials seam; the plugin falls back to the `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` environment variable **only when the credentials service itself is unavailable** — if credentials exists but holds no such key, the environment variable is not consulted. When no key resolves (for example an install signed in with a DeepSeek *account*), the pill keeps showing the billing period and the session cost, and only the balance is absent.\n\n## Install\n\nFrom the plugin market (search `dsh-cost`), or from a terminal:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile <profile> add dsh-cost-pill\n```\n\nYou can also install from the GitHub source: `dsh plugin --profile <profile> add github:Arun1016/dsh-cost`.\n\n> Note: the bare npm name `dsh-cost` belongs to an unrelated project; this plugin is published under the `@arun_1016/` scope, so the two cannot be confused.\n\n## Configuration\n\n```yaml\n- id: cost-stats\n  name: dsh-cost\n  config:\n    holidays: ['2026-01-01']   # statutory holidays bill off-peak all day\n```\n\n`holidays` is the only Config field. It defaults to the built-in 2026 PRC statutory-holiday table (State Council notice 国办发明电〔2025〕7号), as Beijing-local `YYYY-MM-DD` dates. A new year is a Config edit, not a code change.\n\n## Billing model\n\nModel prices are CNY per million tokens, and every figure below is a **peak** rate — off-peak is exactly half, per the official rule. Search and Fetch are billed per request instead, listed at the end of the table.\n\n| Item | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Flash (from 2026-09-10 12:00 Beijing) | peak `2 / 0.04 / 8` = uncached input / cache-hit input / output |\n| Flash (before the price cut) | `3.0 / 0.1 / 9.0`, same three buckets |\n| Pro (`deepseek-v4-pro`, before 2026-09-14 12:00 Beijing) | `9.0 / 0.3 / 27.0`, same three buckets |\n| Peak window | workdays `09:00–12:00` and `14:00–18:00` |\n| Off-peak | everything else; weekends and statutory holidays all day, including a weekend that holiday adjustment turns into a workday |\n| Clock used | the local clock of the machine running dsh — the official windows are Beijing time, so the reading is only exact on a Beijing-time host |\n| pro→flash routing | billed as Flash from 2026-09-14 12:00 Beijing |\n| `inputTokens` | uncached input; cache writes bill at the uncached rate |\n| reasoning | subset of output, not billed separately |\n| Search / Fetch calls | ¥5 per 1,000 successful requests (¥0.005 each), independent of the peak / off-peak window |\n| Web billing start | 2026-11-01 00:00 Beijing; earlier successful calls cost nothing and display as \"Free\" |\n| Successful call | Search returned a non-empty `results` array; Fetch returned page content; failures, empty searches and timeouts are free |\n| Call counting | the session log's `web_search` / `web_fetch` tool calls; one multi-query `web_search` counts its distinct queries |\n| Scope | the session's own events (excluding any fork-inherited prefix) plus the own events of every descendant subagent session it spawned |\n| Subagent identification | header lineage carrying `origin: subagent`, at any depth; a user fork is an independent conversation and never counts |\n| Subagent annotation | with subagents, the session-cost label reads \"(incl. subagents)\" and a small note names how many sessions are included; their cost is never a separate line, it is folded into the amounts above |\n\nThe Search / Fetch price and billing start come from the official [price page](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/zh-cn/quick_start/pricing) and the [web search & fetch guide](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/zh-cn/guides/search) (announced 2026-10-17).\n\n## Privacy\n\n- No telemetry, no analytics, no third-party endpoints.\n- The only outbound request is `https://api.deepseek.com/user/balance`, authenticated with your key; it times out after 15 s.\n- The browser half only reads the host route `/api/dsh-balance` — once per session step, plus a 60 s poll. It never contacts a third-party endpoint itself.\n- This plugin never writes the key to disk, and balances are cached in memory only.\n\n## Known limitations\n\n- While the session is attached the host folds usage per request, so a span across the price cut, the routing change or a peak boundary keeps its own rate table. A **detached** session is priced by the host as one aggregate at the current Flash rates and carries **no** estimate marker; the browser half's own fallback estimate uses the same current rates and is marked `(估)` in Chinese / `(est)` in English.\n- Web search / fetch fees are inferred from the session log's `web_search` / `web_fetch` tool calls: the host does not load a detached session's log and keeps no per-query results, so **detached sessions** and the **local fallback estimate** omit this fee; a log trimmed by compaction undercounts too.\n- A multi-query `web_search` whose queries partly return nothing cannot be split after the results are merged, so every distinct query is billed (an overcount); a failed call bills nothing, but sibling requests that had already succeeded in the same batch cannot be counted (an undercount).\n- A web fee is priced by when the tool result landed, so a request straddling 2026-11-01 00:00 Beijing can land on either side of the billing start by seconds.\n- Subagent spend depends on dsh's session-query service: without it only subagents still resident in memory are counted, so a finished and released subagent is missed.\n- Closed subagents are read from their persisted logs and cached by session id (256 entries). A log that cannot be read (format migration, corruption) is skipped.\n- Running subagents are folded from memory on each read; a subagent that finishes and is released between two cost polls may lag by one poll interval.\n- A fork-inherited prefix is excluded from the session's cost (it was already billed to the parent), and a user fork is a separate conversation that never counts.\n- Calls are counted by tool name, not by the underlying provider. The shipped profile uses DeepSeek's Search / Fetch APIs, where this matches the official bill; with a different search or fetch provider the plugin still counts the calls and would show uncounted calls as billed.\n- Every reading is conditional: a missing balance hides only that segment; a cost of exactly `¥0.00` hides the cost segment; and when the host route is missing or errors, the whole pill disappears silently, with no placeholder and no error message. After a failure it stops per-step polling and keeps only the 60 s poll.\n- Amounts always print with a `¥` prefix, regardless of the account currency the API reports. Balance uses 2 decimals; session costs use 2 decimals, or 4 below `¥0.01`; web call fees use 3 decimals (the ¥0.005 unit — three calls read `¥0.015`, not a two-decimal `¥0.01`).\n- The per-model breakdown appears only when the host can fold the session by model, and model ids are normalised (for example `deepseek-v4-flash` and `deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp` both display as `deepseek-flash`).\n- Balance failures are silent: no key, an invalid key, a network error and the 15 s timeout all produce a `200` response with no `balance_infos` field, and that empty result is cached for 30 s as well.\n- The balance cache is process-wide and shared across sessions; it is only invalidated by a different key, so a top-up can take up to 30 s to appear.\n- Model ids the plugin does not recognise are priced with the Flash table.\n- Costs accumulate per request, so rounding may differ from the account ledger.\n- Events without a model source or usage are skipped for token cost; web calls are folded separately from their own events.\n- The popup has no height cap and does not share the official pills' mutual-exclusion state, so it can stay open alongside another popup.\n- The built-in holiday table covers 2026 only.\n\n## Development\n\nSource lives in `src/` (host half `index.ts`, client half `client/`). It is built with the official dsh monorepo toolchain: `tsconfig.*.json` and `tsdown.config.ts` reference the monorepo through relative paths (`../../../tsconfig.base.json`, `../../client/tsdown.client.ts`), so building requires placing this package back into that tree — the repository cannot be built standalone.\n\nThe published package carries `lib/` and `cordis.patch.yml`, plus `package.json`, both READMEs and `LICENSE` (npm always includes those).\n\n## License\n\nMIT — see [LICENSE](LICENSE).\n"
    },
